<p>
  A <a href="https://trix-editor.org">Trix</a> editor bound to the room's
  document with <a href="https://github.com/jpcamara/y-trix">y-trix</a>. The
  whole document is one <code>Y.Text</code> named <code>trix</code>, in the
  shape of Trix's own model: text with its attributes, and a formatted
  <code>"\n"</code> at the end of each block. Pressing Enter inserts one
  character and joining two blocks deletes one, so two people editing around
  the same line break both keep their text.
</p>
<p>
  The server reads the same document without a browser: <code>Y::Trix</code>
  renders the <code>Y.Text</code> to the HTML Trix itself saves, which is what
  Action Text stores. Open the panel under the editor to see it.
</p>
<p>
  Undo and redo only take back your own changes. Other people's carets and
  selections come through awareness, which the server passes along without
  saving.
</p>
